---
// DRAFT -- not linked from the live nav. Rebuild of Common Concerns as an
// interactive concern-finder instead of a static two-column FAQ (which
// needed a separate "mobile carousel" hack to work on phones at all).
// Same 18 questions, same answer content verbatim -- the change is entirely
// in how you get to an answer: check what you're actually wondering about
// and the list re-sorts, the same interaction language as the facet panels
// on Symptom Guide and Cause Library, so this page finally feels like part
// of that family instead of a leftover static FAQ page next to them.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Common Concerns — TLS Foundations';
const summary =
  "\"Foundation repair Albuquerque,\" \"foundation repair cost,\" \"free foundation inspection\" -- these are among the most expensive search terms in New Mexico, because contractors pay for them knowing homeowners search when they're worried and don't know where to turn. This page answers the eighteen questions behind those searches directly -- cost, warning signs, settlement vs. heave, insurance coverage, warranties, how to choose a company -- instead of routing that worry into a sales call. Click any question to see the honest answer, no contact form required first.";
const description =
  "Eighteen questions New Mexico homeowners actually search for. Answered honestly -- cost, signs, settlement vs. heave, insurance, warranties, and more.";

const serviceAreaText = `This page exists because the most common foundation repair search terms in New Mexico — foundation repair Albuquerque, foundation repair cost, signs of foundation problems, free foundation inspection — lead homeowners to sales calls, not answers. TLS Foundations is a New Mexico foundation repair contractor. We answer these questions honestly because homeowners who understand their situation make better decisions, ask better questions, and are better to work with. The eighteen questions on this page cover foundation repair cost in New Mexico, how to recognize foundation problems, the difference between settlement and heave, when foundation repair is not the right answer, how to choose a foundation contractor, what expansive soil does to a house, whether homeowners insurance covers foundation repair, and what happens when the wrong repair method is used. If your question isn't here, call or text — you reach the owner.`;

// Facet groups -- "what's actually on your mind," not the questions
// themselves. Checking one or more re-sorts the list below so the closest
// matches surface first, same scoring pattern as the Symptom Guide/Cause
// Library facet panels.
const facetGroups = [
  { id: 'money', label: 'Cost, insurance, or warranty' },
  { id: 'diagnosis', label: "What's actually wrong, or how serious it is" },
  { id: 'trust', label: 'Whether a contractor is being straight with me' },
  { id: 'timing', label: 'Whether to act now or wait' },
  { id: 'repair', label: 'What the repair itself involves' },
  { id: 'selling', label: 'Selling the house' },
];

