---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  footer="full"
  ogImage="/images/common-concerns-hero.webp"
  summary={summary}
  pageName="Common Concerns"
  nextPage={{ path: '/foundation-repair-methods', name: 'Foundation Repair Methods' }}
  footerProps={{
    serviceAreaLabel: "Six methods (not to mention a couple others we have up our sleeves). The right one depends on your soil.",
    serviceAreaText,
  }}
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <img class="hero-photo" src="/images/common-concerns-hero.webp" alt="New Mexico adobe home foundation" fetchpriority="high" />
    <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="tls-hero-wrap">
      <div class="tls-hero-box">
        <span class="tls-hero-headline">Google says these are important.</span>
        <span class="tls-hero-sub">(So we answered them.)</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="cc-page">
    <div class="cc-container">
      <div class="cc-header">
        <h1 class="cc-title">Common Concerns</h1>
        <p class="cc-description">Eighteen questions New Mexico homeowners actually search for. Check what's actually on your mind and we'll sort what's most useful to the top — or just scroll, it's only eighteen.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mission-note">
        <p>The most common search terms for foundation repair in New Mexico are: "Foundation repair Albuquerque." "Foundation repair Rio Rancho." "Foundation repair Santa Fe." "Foundation repair Las Cruces." Those are among the most expensive search terms in New Mexico — contractors pay for them because homeowners search them when they're worried and don't know where to turn. Every click on that keyword costs someone money. This page doesn't. It exists because the answer to that search shouldn't be a sales call — it should be honest information about what's happening under your house, what it means, and what your options actually are. That's what's here.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="facet-panel" id="facetPanel">
        <div class="facet-panel-head">
          <span class="facet-panel-label">What's actually on your mind? (check all that apply)</span>
          <p class="facet-panel-sub">Check any that fit and the closest matches move to the top. Leave it blank and all eighteen show in the order homeowners ask them most.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="facet-options">
          {facetGroups.map((g) => (
            <label class="facet-chip">
              <input type="checkbox" name="concern-tag" value={g.id} />
              {g.label}
            </label>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="facet-actions">
          <button type="button" id="facetClear" class="facet-clear" hidden>Clear all</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="matched-lead" id="matchedLead" hidden></p>

      <div class="concern-list" id="concernList">
        {concerns.map((c) => (
          <div
            class="concern-card"
            id={c.id}
            data-tags={c.tags.join(',')}
          >
            <button type="button" class="concern-head" data-toggle aria-expanded="false">
              <div class="concern-head-text">
                <span class="concern-teaser">{c.teaser}</span>
                <h2 class="concern-q">{c.q}</h2>
              </div>
              <span class="concern-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"></line><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"></line></svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="concern-body">
              <div class="concern-body-inner">
                <p>{c.p}</p>
                <div class="nm-note">NM context: {c.nmNote}</div>
                <div class="industry-note">{c.industryNote}</div>
                <div class="card-links">
                  {c.primaryLinks.length > 0 && (
                    <div class="primary-links">
                      {c.primaryLinks.map((l) => <a href={l.href} class="card-link">{l.text}</a>)}
                    </div>
                  )}
                  <div class="related-terms"><span>Related terms</span>{c.relatedTerms.map((t) => <a href={t.href}>{t.text}</a>)}</div>
                  <div class="related-faq"><span>Related questions</span>{c.relatedFaq.map((f) => <a href={f.href} class="related-faq-link" data-target={f.href.split('#')[1]}>{f.text}</a>)}</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="matrix-footer">
      <p>If you don't see your question here, <a href="/contact-us">contact us directly</a> — you reach the owner.</p>
      <p class="matrix-footer-sub">Or watch the <a href="/homeowner-decision-series">Homeowner Decision Series</a> — four short videos on these same questions, on camera.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

